What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/eem/calibrate
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Write 1 to run BSP EEM INIT01/INIT02 on BIG/L/LL/CCI banks and
		start advisory MON sampling. All three CPU clusters must be
		active, their current frequencies and CCI at most 750000 kHz.
		Otherwise the request fails with EBUSY. The CPUfreq supplier lock
		and CPU read lock protect a temporary 1 V calibration supply and
		the exact restoration of manual rails/modes. OPPs are not changed.
		Write 0 to stop EEM and restore the saved writable registers.
		Suspend stops MON; resume reruns INIT02 using cached DC offsets.
		Loading the driver alone does not perform a calibration.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/eem/state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 Bring-up <admin@taterli.com>
Description:
		Read-only calibration/MON status, runs, samples, failures, last
		error and eFuse ATE version. Rejected calibration requests count
		as failures. Each bank reports DC/age offsets, status, packed
		VOP voltage codes, MTS/BTS and eight frequency percentages.
		Results are advisory: automatic_voltage=0 and the manual CPUfreq
		curve remains the voltage owner. Raw codes are not measured rails.
